# a glued operator joins its neighbours into one item of a space list (decision glued-binds-tighter): [a+b c] is
# [(a+b), c]; gluing changes item boundaries, never precedence; the spaced form beside a phrase of values is refused
'a = 1; b = 2; c = 3; [a+b c]'	[3, 3]
'a = 1; b = 2; c = 3; [a*b c a-b]'	[2, 3, -1]
'1+2 * 3'	7
'a = 1; b = 2; c = 3; [a + b c]'	error	[a + b c] reads neither way: [a+b c] or [a + b, c]
'f(x) := x * 2; a = 1; [a + f 3]'	[7]
'a-b = 5; c = 1; [a-b c]'	[5, 1]
'f(x) := x * 2; a = 1; y = a+f 3; y'	7
